ivity property by relying on the quenched box-crossing property proved by Ahlberg, Griffiths, Morris and Tassion [AGMT16].\nL17: Intermediate results also include the study of quenched and annealed notions of pivotal events and the extension of the quenched box-crossing property of [AGMT16] to the near-critical regime.\nL18: Comments:  | 68 pages, 13 figures, minor changes\nL19: Subjects:  | Probability (math.PR); Mathematical Physics (math-ph)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:1806.08452 [math.PR]\nL21:    | (or cite10†arXiv:1806.08452v3 [math.PR] for this version)\nL22:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1806.08452†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Hugo Vanneuville [cite12†view email ]\nL26: cite5†[v1] Thu, 21 Jun 2018 23:22:51 UTC (494 KB)\nL27: cite13†[v2] Fri, 28 Sep 2018 15:12:22 UTC (681 KB)\nL28: [v3] Tue, 30 Apr 2019 16:18:17 UTC (588 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Annealed scaling relations for Voronoi percolation, by Hugo Vanneuville\nL35: \nL36:   * cite7†View PDF L37:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite14†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite15†view license L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: math.PR\nL44: \nL45: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L46: \nL47: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2018-06 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite21†math L52: cite22†math-ph L53: cite23†math.MP L54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * cite24†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L58:   * cite25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L59:   * cite26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L60: \nL61: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL62: \nL63: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL64: \nL65: [Button: ×]\nL66: \nL67: loading...\nL68: \nL69: Data provided by:\nL70: \nL71: ### Bookmark\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL74: # Bibliographic